# Architecture (recap-engine)

## Package boundary

| `@recap-engine/core` | `@recap-engine/react` |
|----------------------|------------------------|
| Types, enums, reducers, `prepareRecap`, formatters, `resolveValue` | DOM, hooks, CSS, context, layouts, primitives |
| Framework-agnostic | React 19 peer |

- Do not put JSX, DOM APIs, or React lifecycle into `core`
- Do not reimplement `playerReducer` / scene contracts in `react`
- UI helpers (`cn`, `backgroundStyle`, motion→class maps) stay in `react`

## Layers in react

- `primitives/` — atoms; no `SceneDefinition` / scene switch
- `layouts/` — scene orchestration + `resolveValue`; not public by default
- `Recap/` — player shell, gestures, lifecycle
- `hooks/` — reusable, domain-agnostic hooks only
- Feature hooks that use `useRecap` live next to the feature (`Recap/useAutoplay.ts`)

## Public API

- Export only through package `src/index.ts`
- Export: `Recap`, `RecapProps`, `useRecap`, selected primitives, `registerScene`
- Do not export layouts, `SceneRenderer`, `RecapShell`, or internal player hooks
- Re-export from `core` only a documented stable subset — consumers may depend on `@recap-engine/core` directly
- Internal helpers (`variantClass`, `cn` if unused by hosts) stay private

## Barrels

- Feature folders either all have `index.ts` or none (except package root)
- Outside the package, deep imports into internals are forbidden
